WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:03.280
- What's a good way to teach math?

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:05.620
- [Respondent] Chronologically.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.453
- The people.

00:00:06.453 --> 00:00:09.910
- The people behind the theorems, yeah.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.260
Their cousins and their
nieces and their faces

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:17.510
and how they jump from the bath tub

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.087
when they scream "Eureka!"

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.733
And run naked in town.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.840
- So, you're almost educated
as a historian of math?

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.540
- [Respondent] No, we just
get a glimpse of that history

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.250
together with a theorem, so
every year exercise in math

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.803
was connected with a person.

00:00:36.189 --> 00:00:40.070
At the time of the person, the period.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.170
- [Interviewer] The period
also mathematically speaking.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.620
- Mathematically speaking,
yes, not the politics.

